	Yes, but they'll still fade after too many readings, and I take it
that the OP's idea is that the spellstone won't.  Personally, I like it,
but I have a feeling it would be a little unbalancing.  Maybe if it 
required an item with charges, like a magic marker...  I also wonder
how you would use the spellstone, since to read something you either 
have to have it in your inventory or you have to be standing on the
square with it.  This would mean that to read a spell-boulder, you 
either have to be a giant or you have to be naked and squeezed into the
square with it, which would make them not very useful.  I assume that
if you turned the boulder into a giant chunk of meat, it would not
become a spell-steak.  *g*

	Personally, I wouldn't mind seeing the magic system made a
little more complex - maybe require certain objects or conditions for 
certain powerful spells, like "you must have a garnet and a bat corpse 
to cast spell X", or "you must be wielding a dagger and be next to a 
water square to cast spell Y".  Not for everything, of course, that 
would make spellcasting far too difficult.


